    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28935" root="عز" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْتَزٌّ</span></b>  is syn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسْتَعِزٌّ</span>. (TA.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنَا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْتَزٌّ بِبَنِى فُلَانٍ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِهِمْ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسْتَعِزٌّ</span></b>  [<i>I reckon myself
strong by means of the sons of such a one</i>]. (A.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرَسٌ مُعْتَزَّةٌ</span> <i>A mare having thick and strong
flesh.</i> (TA.)

